# Caddy sits behind pihole-tailscale's TCPForward+TerminateTLS serve config.
# Tailscale terminates TLS on the tailnet-facing side (443) using its own
# automatic cert for pihole.${TS_TAILNET_DOMAIN}, then forwards the
# decrypted plaintext HTTP as a raw TCP stream to Caddy on 8444 — this port
# is never published to the host, it's only reachable via the shared
# network namespace (network_mode: service:pihole) from pihole-tailscale's loopback.
#
# Caddy exists here purely to do the actual HTTP-level reverse proxying,
# since tailscaled's own built-in Web/Proxy serve mode is documented as
# 5-10x slower under concurrent load (tailscale/tailscale#18307) — enough
# to make Pi-hole's admin UI hang loading its own CSS/JS assets. Caddy
# doesn't need its own TLS cert or config beyond this — the tailnet-facing
# TLS is entirely Tailscale's job.
:8444 {
	reverse_proxy 127.0.0.1:80
}
